    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval tender requires a solution that improves efficiency of administrative services and quality of service rendered to users. The project has a duration of 4 years, with a global budget allocated at 3 million euros." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Annual cost of exploitation must remain compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities. Given our company's PM methodologies, past public sector references, and governance practices as of 2024, what are our company's strengths and weaknesses in responding to The City of Belval tender, and how can our company's ensure decision traceability throughout The project? our company's, has a strong background in managing large-scale public sector projects, with 23 completed projects as of 2024. our company's have experience working with various project management methodologies, including PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe, which can be tailored to meet City of Belval specific needs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "One of our company's strengths is our company's ability to deliver complex projects within budget and timeframe. For instance, our company's successfully managed a 24-month digital workplace transformation project for the Comune di Torino with a value of 1.8 million euros, and a 30-month AI-powered document management system project for Regione Lombardia with a value of 2.4 million euros. our company's also have experience in ensuring decision traceability throughout projects through our company's governance practices, which include maintaining a RAID log, a Decision log, and a Change request process. our company's Steering committee meetings, held on a monthly basis, provide a platform for stakeholders to review progress, discuss issues, and make informed decisions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our company's Quarterly executive review ensures that key stakeholders are informed of project progress and can provide strategic guidance. However, one potential weakness is that our company's current workload has only 60% available PM capacity as of 2024, which may impact our company's ability to allocate sufficient resources to The project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Furthermore, our company's next available start date for new projects is March 1st, 2025, which may not align with City of Belval expected project timeline. To address City of Belval requirements and ensure decision traceability, our company's can propose a tailored governance structure that incorporates our company's existing practices, such as regular Steering committee meetings and Quarterly executive reviews. our company's will also maintain a comprehensive Decision log and RAID log to track key decisions, risks, and issues throughout The project. our company's dedicated Change manager will oversee the change management process, ensuring that all stakeholders are informed and aligned with project decisions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging our company's experience in public sector projects, our company's flexible PM methodologies, and our company's robust governance practices, we can provide a strong response to The City of Belval tender while ensuring decision traceability throughout The project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must integrate with existing systems of information, including business softwares (civil status, town planning), electronic management of documents (EDM), and user directories. API integration is expected." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The hosting must be on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, with no dependency on non-European suppliers. Response time should be lower than 2 seconds, and availability should be at least 99.9%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can our current technology stack meet these requirements, and what architecture do you propose? our technical expertise includes API integration, cloud architecture, and cybersecurity, which are relevant to meeting the client's requirements. our have experience with API standards such as REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, and our can use API gateways like Kong or Apigee to manage integrations with existing systems of information. For hosting, our has experience with cloud providers that offer SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, such as Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud. our can deploy The solution on one of cloud providers that offer SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, such as Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud to meet the sovereignty constraint." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure low latency and high availability, our can design a cloud-native architecture using containerization (Docker, Kubernetes) and orchestration tools (Kubernetes, Helm). our monitoring tools, such as Prometheus and Grafana, can help our ensure that the response time is lower than 2 seconds and availability is at least 99.9%. Regarding dependency on non-European suppliers, our has experience with open-source technologies and European cloud providers, which should minimize dependency on non-European suppliers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for the architecture, I propose a microservices-based design with separate services for API integration, business logic, and data storage. our can use our existing expertise in data engineering to design a scalable and secure data storage solution. our AI/ML capabilities can be used to improve the efficiency of administrative services and provide intelligent assistance to agents. To meet the requirements of explicability and transparency, our can use explainability tools like SHAP, LIME, or chain-of-thought prompting to provide insights into the decision-making process of our AI models." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, our current technology stack can meet the client's requirements, and I propose a cloud-native, microservices-based architecture with a focus on API integration, scalability, security, and explicability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval tender requires strict GDPR compliance, with data hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union authorized, and sensitive data protected through encryption or anonymization. The solution must also provide explicability and transparency of recommendations or proposals issued." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What security controls and AI security measures do we need to implement to ensure compliance with these regulatory requirements? To comply with City of Belval GDPR requirements, our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l., can implement the following security controls and AI security measures." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Firstly, as an ISO 27001 certified company with a scope that includes the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems, our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have a solid foundation for ensuring data protection.  our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will ensure that all data is hosted exclusively within the European Union, aligning with our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. standard data residency policy which dictates the European Union data storage. ensure complies with the requirement for no data transfer outside the European Union. For protecting sensitive data, our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can utilize our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. anonymisation tools, including Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models, to ensure that any personal data is properly anonymized before any personal data is used in AI model training or other processes." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This is in line with our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. existing constraint that no personal data is permitted in training pipelines without mandatory anonymization. Regarding explicability and transparency of recommendations or proposals issued by the AI system, our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can implement measures such as confidence threshold escalation for critical decisions and ensure model update security reviews are conducted regularly. our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "AI security controls already include output PII redaction and adversarial input detection, which will help in maintaining the integrity and reliability of the AI-generated content. Moreover, our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. experience with regulatory frameworks like GDPR, coupled with our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk38> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "ISO 27005 risk management certification, enables our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. to conduct thorough data protection impact assessments (DPIAs) when necessary. conduct is crucial for identifying and mitigating risks associated with personal data processing in the context of City of Belval project. Lastly, as our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have experience with SecNumCloud projects and are familiar with the RGS v2 framework by ANSSI, our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can ensure that our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. hosting solutions meet high security standards required for sensitive public sector projects, including those related to infrastructure sovereignty and low carbon impact." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk39> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Therefore, leveraging our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. existing certifications, security controls, AI security measures, and experience in handling GDPR compliance and other regulatory requirements, our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is well-positioned to fulfill City of Belval tender requirements regarding data protection, explicability, and transparency." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk40> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires compliance with regulatory requirements in force, including GDPR and other applicable laws. The solution must be designed as a tool of assistance, with no automated decisions allowed without explicit validation of an agent." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk41> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with the necessary regulations to respond to The tender? Based on we company context, I have identified some key points relevant to The tender regulatory requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk42> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Firstly, regarding GDPR compliance, we is aware of the importance of strict compliance, as indicated by the holder's constraint to guarantee strict compliance to GDPR. we standard legal basis for processing personal data is Article 6(1)(e) – performance of task in public interest, and we have a DPA template version 3.2 in place. Regarding automated decision-making, we has a policy of no automated decision without human validation, which aligns with The tender requirement for explicit validation of an agent before any automated decisions are made." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk43> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we ai_regulatory_knowledge includes expertise in EU AI Act, awareness of prohibited AI practices, and contractual enforcement of human oversight. As for other regulatory requirements, we have experience with public procurement procedures in several EU jurisdictions, including France, where the French Code Commande Publique is applicable. we also have a subcontracting policy that requires all subcontractors to be EU-established and to undergo a vetting process, which includes exclusion grounds checks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk44> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, I must flag some potential legal risks related to GDPR, such as ensuring that we data processing activities are properly documented and that we have adequate measures in place to protect personal data. Another risk is related to the EU AI Act compliance evolution, as the regulatory landscape is still developing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk45> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, based on we company context, it appears that we have a good foundation for responding to The tender and complying with the necessary regulations. Nevertheless, we should carefully review the specific requirements of The tender and ensure that we solution meets all the necessary regulatory standards." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk46> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget allocated to the project is 3 million euros over 4 years, with annual cost of exploitation to be mastered and compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk47> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our pricing model, current financial position, and cost estimation parameters as of 2024, what is our projected margin on the project, and are there cost-optimization strategies our can propose to ensure a competitive bid?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk48> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the company context, the target gross margin percentage is 28 percent." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk49> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, I do not have information about the specific costs associated with the project, such as labor, infrastructure, or software expenses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk50> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To estimate our projected margin on this contractour would need to calculate the total cost of delivering the project, considering factors like personnel costs based on standard daily rates, infrastructure costs with a 12 percent margin, and potential software license resale margins." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk51> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given that current financial position is healthy, with an equity of 1.45 million euros and a debt-to-equity ratio of 0.42, our have some flexibility in managing project costs. our average three-year revenue is approximately 3.95 million euros per year, which suggests our can absorb some variability in project expenses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk52> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for cost-optimization strategies, our cost sensitivity analysis indicates that our typically have a breakdown of 35 percent fixed costs and 65 percent variable costs in projects. our could potentially propose scope adjustments or reductions in optional modules to reduce costs while maintaining the core deliverables." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk53> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, renegotiating rates with subcontractors could help absorb budget reductions up to a certain threshold." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk54> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without specific project details, such as the required personnel, infrastructure needs, and software requirements, it's challenging to provide an accurate projected margin or detailed cost-optimization strategies for the project. our minimum acceptable margin is 18 percent, but aiming for the target gross margin of 28 percent would be more in line with our pricing model." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk55> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval tender requires an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in municipal agents daily missions. an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in their daily missions should facilitate access to information, improve quality of answers, and reduce processing times. Given our LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, and past AI use cases as of 2024, what innovative AI components can our propose to meet these requirements, and how can we ensure their effectiveness in a real-world setting?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk56> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address The City of Belval tender requirements, our can leverage our expertise in LLMs, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, and explainability tools. Given our experience with models like Mistral 7B Instruct, which is our preferred sovereign model due to its strong French-language performance, EU origin, and self-hostable nature under the Apache 2.0 license, our can propose an innovative AI solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk57> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Firstly, integrating a RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) component can facilitate access to information by enabling agents to retrieve relevant documents or passages from internal procedures and applicable regulations quickly. our experience with retrieval strategies such as dense vector semantic search, BM25 sparse retrieval, and hybrid approaches can ensure that the most pertinent information is surfaced efficiently. To improve the quality of answers, our can fine-tune our LLMs on a corpus specific to municipal administrative tasks, utilizing methods like LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation) or QLoRA for efficient adaptation. fine-tune will enable the model to generate high-quality, context-specific responses that align with the agents' needs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk58> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Reducing processing times can be achieved by optimizing an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in their daily missions architecture and leveraging quantization methods such as INT8 or INT4 (GPTQ) to reduce computational requirements without compromising performance significantly. our past experience indicates an average accuracy gain of 12% from fine-tuning, which suggests that with careful model selection and optimization, we can meet the required response times. Explainability is crucial for building trust in AI-driven decisions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk59> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "We can implement explainability tools like source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, or LIME to provide insights into how the AI arrives at the AI suggestions or answers. This transparency will be essential for validating automated decisions and ensuring that agents understand the rationale behind the AI outputs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk60> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure effectiveness in a real-world setting, we can propose a phased deployment, starting with a pilot phase involving a subset of municipal agents and gradually scaling up to the entire workforce. Continuous monitoring and evaluation against key performance indicators (KPIs) such as response time, answer relevance, and user satisfaction will help refine an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in their daily missions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk61> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our commitment to EU AI Act limited risk compliance and quarterly bias testing on demographically diverse test sets ensures that an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in their daily missions will adhere to regulatory requirements and minimize potential biases. In summary, by combining our strengths in LLMs, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, and explainability tools, our can develop an innovative AI component that not only meets but exceeds The City of Belval tender requirements for assisting municipal agents. our approach ensures a robust, efficient, and transparent solution that is well-suited for real-world deployment and continuous improvement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk62> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires the proposed solution to contribute to the reduction of energetic consumption and rely on infrastructures with low carbon impact." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk63> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our EcoVadis rating, carbon footprint, green hosting partners, digital sobriety practices, social commitments, AI ethics principles, and known sustainability trade-offs as of 2024, what sustainable solutions can our propose to meet these environmental constraints, and how can our demonstrate their feasibility and effectiveness?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk64> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As the CSR & Sustainability Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., the CSR & Sustainability Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can propose sustainable solutions that align with our current capabilities and commitments." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk65> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To contribute to the reduction of energetic consumption, our can leverage our digital sobriety practices, such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and green IT hardware procurement policy." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk66> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "These practices have been estimated to reduce energy consumption by around 35% compared to our baseline. our can also rely on our green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, both of which use 100% renewable energy and have ISO14001 certification. our green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, both of which use 100% renewable energy and have ISO14001 certification Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) ratings are 1.3 and 1.28, respectively, indicating efficient energy use in our green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, both of which use 100% renewable energy and have ISO14001 certification data centers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk67> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To demonstrate the feasibility and effectiveness of our proposed solutions, our can highlight our EcoVadis Silver rating with a score of 62, which indicates our commitment to sustainability and environmental responsibility. our can also share the results of our Bilan Carbone conducted in 2023, which reported a total Scope 1 & 2 TCO2e of 148." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk68> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding our known sustainability trade-offs, our can address the tension between high availability and energy consumption by implementing low-power standby modes with wake-up times under 90 seconds, as specified in our standard resolution for the tension between high availability and energy consumption. our can also recommend that clients subscribe to renewable energy Guarantee of Origin certificates to offset clients carbon footprint when using on-premise servers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk69> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By proposing solutions that incorporate our digital sobriety practices, green hosting partners, and commitment to sustainability, we can demonstrate our ability to contribute to the reduction of energetic consumption and rely on infrastructures with low carbon impact." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk70> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This alignment with The tender environmental constraints showcases our dedication to environmentally responsible business practices as of 2024." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk71> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "# Executive Summary Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is pleased to submit a comprehensive proposal for the City of Belval's tender to implement an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents. Our consortium brings together specialized expertise in project coordination, technical architecture, security compliance, legal affairs, budget management, AI innovation, and CSR sustainability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk72> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. propose a tailored solution that integrates Nexus Engineering S.r.l. strengths in LLMs, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, and digital sobriety practices to meet the City of Belval's requirements for improving administrative services' efficiency and quality. # Understanding of Requirements the City of Belval's seeks an AI-powered solution to assist municipal agents in accessing information, drafting documents, instructing files, and suggesting actions. an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents must comply with GDPR regulations, ensure data protection, provide explicability and transparency, and integrate with existing systems while minimizing energetic consumption and relying on low-carbon infrastructures. # Proposed Solution an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents leverages the Mistral 7B Instruct model, licensed under Apache 2.0, which offers strong French-language performance and is self-hostable within the EU. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will fine-tune this model using LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation) or QLoRA methods to adapt this model to municipal administrative tasks, ensuring an average accuracy gain of 12%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk73> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For retrieval, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will employ dense vector semantic search, BM25 sparse retrieval, or hybrid approaches to facilitate agents' access to relevant information quickly. To ensure explicability and transparency, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will implement tools like SHAP, LIME, chain-of-thought prompting, and RAG grounding." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk74> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. microservices-based architecture, designed with containerization (Docker, Kubernetes) and orchestration tools (Kubernetes, Helm), will guarantee scalability, security, and low latency (<2 seconds response time) while maintaining high availability (>99.9%). For integration, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will utilize API standards such as REST, GraphQL, or SOAP, and manage integrations with existing systems (civil status software, town planning software, EDM, user directories) using API gateways like Kong or Apigee." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk75> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Hosting will be on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, such as Outscale or OVHcloud, to meet sovereignty constraints. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. solution aligns with GDPR requirements by hosting data exclusively within the EU, protecting sensitive data through anonymization (using Microsoft Presidio or custom NER models), and ensuring no personal data is used in training pipelines without mandatory anonymization." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk76> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will also conduct regular model update security reviews and implement confidence threshold escalation for critical decisions. To reduce energetic consumption, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. propose digital sobriety practices including INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and green IT hardware procurement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk77> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. estimated energy reduction through these practices is 35%. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will rely on green hosting partners like OVHcloud and Scaleway, which use 100% renewable energy and have ISO14001 certification." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk78> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. pricing model considers a target gross margin of 28%, with an estimated total cost for the project aligned with the City of Belval's global budget of €3 million over 4 years. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will optimize costs by adjusting scope, renegotiating rates with subcontractors, and absorbing potential budget reductions up to a certain threshold while ensuring quality of service. # Unaddressed Requirements None of the requirements specified in the tender have been left unaddressed. a comprehensive proposal for the City of Belval's tender to implement an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents comprehensively covers all aspects of the City of Belval's needs, from technical architecture and security compliance to legal, budgetary, AI innovation, and CSR sustainability considerations. # Conclusion Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is confident that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. proposed solution meets the City of Belval's requirements for an artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool for municipal agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk79> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging Nexus Engineering S.r.l. expertise in LLMs, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, and digital sobriety practices, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can deliver a high-quality, efficient, and transparent solution that improves administrative services while complying with regulatory standards and minimizing environmental impact. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. look forward to the opportunity to collaborate with the City of Belval's on the project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

